File: lib/OCP/Cmd/Destroy.pm:130,135

Lines 130 and 135 hand-code `eq 'ssh'` for both the CP fallback and the worker-pool teardown. A worker pool whose provider is `local` is silently dropped from the destroy fallback reconstruction, so the local node keeps running (and billing) after `ocp destroy --force`. Replace the literals with `OCP::Provider->known_type($w->{provider} // q())` checks — same pattern as karr #103.

Repro:
1. ocp init --provider local
2. ocp apply
3. ocp destroy --force
Observed: local node is not in the destruction list.
